WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.696
From vague to specific: Move from vague to specific. A good prompt states role, goal, and format. Add constraints like length, tone, and what not to do, and give one short example when helpful.

2
00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:24.878
Structure beats clever wording: Structure beats clever wording. Use headings for goal, inputs, and output format. Ask for checkable outputs, and prefer clear instructions over buzzwords.

3
00:00:25.228 --> 00:00:36.988
Test before you trust: Test before you trust. Try good, bad, and ambiguous inputs. Note failures like missing steps or invented facts, tighten the prompt, then retest.

4
00:00:37.338 --> 00:00:47.154
Your Module 2 next step: Open Prompting Basics in the course viewer. Rewrite one vague request into a structured prompt, and save before and after notes in your starter pack.
